tongue|Mouth organ and language meanings retain separate source ordinals; no inherited single-gene trait claim. Loose tooth and grandmother narrative align in Vietnamese; native tongue remains a linguistic expression rather than anatomy.
web|Spider structure and linked online resources are distinct source-supported nouns. Threads versus museum hours contexts align; definition distinguishes web from all internet services and does not assert every spider uses webs identically.
chew|Food-breaking action demonstrated by slowly chewing bread, with simultaneous listening preserved. Teeth action is not confused with swallowing; transitive and intransitive notes do not impose a tense restriction.
habitual|Repeated established pattern is separated from compulsory or addictive behaviour. Early-arrival example and Vietnamese convey a routine; the gloss is complete and the grammar does not assert every habitual action is negative.
motorcycle|Two-wheel motor vehicle boundary fits parking example; Vietnamese xe máy/mô tô is natural. Ride versus drive note is qualified as ordinary usage rather than an absolute grammatical prohibition or vehicle identity approval.
